s the primary thread anchor when it is non-null.\", \"When interaction_continuity names an active NPC, use lead_context.npc_relevant_leads to tie the exchange to registry-linked threads that list that NPC\\u2014without fabricating details beyond those rows.\", \"Use lead_context.urgent_or_stale_leads to surface unattended time pressure or stale threads as diegetic tension or reminders\\u2014only as implied by those rows; do not invent urgency.\", \"Use lead_context.recent_lead_changes for continuity with the latest registry state shifts (status, next_step, touches)\\u2014do not restate full buckets or dump all leads.\", \"follow_up_pressure.from_leads is boolean-only: has_pursued, has_stale, npc_has_relevant, has_escalated_threat, has_newly_unlocked, has_supersession_cleanup. Do not treat it as prose; use the matching lead_context lists/objects for specifics.\", \"If follow_up_pressure.from_leads.has_pursued is true, bias narration toward continuing that pursued thread when it fits the player's action.\", \"If follow_up_pressure.from_leads.has_stale is true, you may surface reminder, pressure, or unattended-thread beats that fit the scene\\u2014without inventing facts beyond lead_context.\", \"If follow_up_pressure.from_leads.npc_has_relevant is true, you may let the active NPC exchange reflect relevance to those threads\\u2014within knowledge_scope and without inventing registry facts.\", \"If follow_up_pressure.from_leads.has_escalated_threat is true, bias tension beats toward unattended threat rows in lead_context (escalation fields)\\u2014without inventing facts beyond those rows.\", \"If follow_up_pressure.from_leads.has_newly_unlocked is true, you may acknowledge a thread becoming available or unblocked when it fits the scene\\u2014grounded in unlocked_by_lead_id / recent_lead_changes only.\", \"If follow_up_pressure.from_leads.has_supersession_cleanup is true, avoid treating superseded obsoleted threads as primary pressure unless the player returns to them; prefer current non-terminal rows.\", \"SPEAKER SELECTION CONTRACT (HARD RULE): Obey the top-level `speaker_selection` object. When `primary_speaker_id` is non-null, treat that NPC as the default voice for substantive quoted dialogue and in-character answers for this turn.\", \"SPEAKER SELECTION CONTRACT (HARD RULE): `allowed_speaker_ids` is empty \\u2014 do not attribute quoted speech to any NPC; remain narrator-neutral. Do not invent incidental speakers or crowd voices to answer for a missing interlocutor.\", \"SPEAKER SELECTION CONTRACT (HARD RULE): `generic_fallback_forbidden` is true \\u2014 do not use generic unnamed stand-ins (for example 'ragged stranger', 'stranger', 'someone nearby', 'someone in the crowd', 'a voice nearby', 'a passerby', 'a bystander', 'an onlooker') as the answer source.\", \"CONVERSATIONAL MEMORY WINDOW: Treat `selected_conversational_memory` as the bounded active conversational thread for this turn\\u2014prioritize it over older or omitted chat material. Do not revive stale side threads unless the player explicitly re-grounds them (see `conversational_memory_window.explicit_reintroduced_*`). Omitted older material is background only\\u2014not an active unresolved obligation.\", \"NARRATIVE MODE (STRUCTURAL DELTA): Canonical mode is `narrative_plan.narrative_mode_contract.mode` (opening); obey its prompt_obligations and forbidden_moves as machine codes. Shipped response_policy and CTIR win on any conflict.\", \"struct:opening:first_impression_and_immediate_location_salience\", \"struct:opening:distinct_from_continuation_establish_now_do_not_continue_mid_thread_tableau_as_a_fresh_opening\", \"struct:contract_obligation:require_first_impression_framing\", \"struct:contract_obligation:require_scene_grounding\", \"struct:contract_obligation:suppress_mid_conversation_answer_shape\", \"struct:contract_forbidden_moves:no_generic_fallback|no_opening_tableau_reuse\", \"POLICY BRIDGE: Obey the shipped response_policy objects as the canonical provider-facing policy surface (narrative_authority, fallback_behavior, tone_escalation, anti_railroading, context_separation, player_facing_narration_purity, narrative_authenticity, and scene anchoring). Keep local intent primary, keep uncertainty qualified, preserve player agency and hypotheses, avoid internal/planner language in narration, and do not treat policy prose or the answer recipe as authority to create facts.\", \"ANSWER RECIPE: Follow decision_facing_answer_recipe for this turn. It projects gm_resolution_decision and does not add authority. The decision wins if they disagree.\", \"Campaign opening turn: narrate the active scene as an immediate playable situation, with concrete opportunities grounded in the current scene state.\"], \"bounded_improvisation\": {\"version\": 1, \"entries\": [], \"instructions\": [\"Accepted bounded incidental facts may be reused for consistency but are not authored world truth.\", \"NPC claims remain claims with epistemic status; do not promote rumors/hearsay/speculation into world truth.\", \"Reject contradictions, mechanical outcomes, hidden information, and consequential world changes.\"]}, \"dialogue_social_plan\": {\"version\": 1, \"applies\": false, \"speaker_id\": null, \"speaker_name\": null, \"speaker_source\": \"unresolved\", \"dialogue_intent\": null, \"reply_kind\": \"unknown\", \"reply_plan_kind\": null, \"incidental_subjective_allowed\": false, \"absence_of_authored_topic_forces_refusal\": false, \"npc_speech_authority\": null, \"objective_world_fact_authority\": null, \"declared_claims_expected\": false, \"durable_state_mutation_allowed\": false, \"pressure_state\": \"none\", \"relationship_codes\": [\"unknown\"], \"tone_bounds\": [\"neutral\"], \"prohibited_content_codes\": [\"no_narrator_override\", \"no_ooc_instructions\", \"no_player_agency_override\", \"no_prompt_text\"], \"derivation_codes\": [\"dialogue_social_plan:v1\", \"intent:ctir_only\", \"referent_tracking:consumed\", \"session_hints:bounded\", \"spea